From 1ce762ba46395db4a3fcde29db690db800f5b43a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:33:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: escalate stranded parked cards once per park
 episode

A card parked in triage/blocked past kanban.stranded_park_seconds (7200) with no
valid human_request and no live owner now gets one generated approval request
(promote / archive / re-scope), an optional triage-desk binding
(kanban.triage_owner_chat) and a stranded_park_escalated event per park episode
(kanban_stranded_park, run last in sweep_blocked_cards, isolated from the tick).
The sweep does real work at most once per
kanban.stranded_sweep_interval_seconds (300) per board per process, and opens
each state.db at most once per pass (Liveness cache).

A live owner is an unreleased chat link whose chat is live (local: state.db row
present, not archived/auto_archived/hidden, and open or active within
kanban.stranded_owner_idle_seconds; remote: assumed live) or an open
spend-decision supervisor card for the current spend episode. The spend decision
producer no longer binds or counts a dead local chat, so it falls through to the
supervisor card.

Co-Authored-By: Contributor <contributor@example.com>
